BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Film Screening: Mean Streets — Berkeley/San Francisco
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-08:00":20261106T160000
DTSTAMP:20261107T130934Z
UID:ce7f6d4936f119ff578e871b2304@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Films\,Berkeley/San Francisco\,United States
DESCRIPTION:Set during the Feast of San Gennaro in the Italian neighborhoo
 d where Martin Scorsese grew up\, and populated with characters and situat
 ions based on the neighborhood’s inhabitants\, Mean Streets is an early 
 distillation of the themes that would define the director’s career. Char
 lie (Harvey Keitel) is torn between his devout Catholicism\, his commitmen
 t to his volatile friend Johnny Boy (Robert De Niro)\, a romantic entangle
 ment with Johnny’s cousin Teresa\, and opportunities offered by his crim
 e boss uncle. Crackling with creative energy\, this now iconic neo-noir is
  inflected with influences from French New Wave\, cinema verité\, and Ame
 rican independent filmmakers like Kenneth Anger\, John Cassave\nCategory: 
 Films\nOriginal listing: https://events.berkeley.edu/BAMPFA/event/331138-f
 ilm-screening-mean-streets
LOCATION:BAMPFA\, BAMPFA
STATUS:CANCELLED
URL:https://events.berkeley.edu/BAMPFA/event/331138-film-screening-mean-st
 reets
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:berkeley-arts
END:VEVENT
