BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Film Screening: Harakiri — Berkeley/San Francisco
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-08:00":20261106T190000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-08:00":20261106T200000
DTSTAMP:20261107T130934Z
UID:61f9a184e14f264dedd9b205fa67@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Films\,Berkeley/San Francisco\,United States
DESCRIPTION:Masaki Kobayashi harnesses the breathtaking beauty of black-an
 d-white\, widescreen cinematography to create an abstract epic. Starring T
 atsuya Nakadai\, the film depicts one man’s desperate attempt to crack t
 he blind\, absolute authority that characterizes the feudal age and\, Koba
 yashi suggests\, our own. In an Edo-period mansion\, the camera inches dow
 n hallways and finds rooms within rooms to explicate a complex flashback n
 arration. In the bloody climax\, the black-robed figures who were caught a
 nd dissected by a stationary camera throughout the film come into their ow
 n as an inexorable prophecy\, like Toru Takemitsu’s haunting music and t
 he words that emerge almost rhythmically from the dialogue\nCategory: Film
 s\nOriginal listing: https://events.berkeley.edu/BAMPFA/event/331139-film-
 screening-harakiri
LOCATION:BAMPFA\, BAMPFA
STATUS:CANCELLED
URL:https://events.berkeley.edu/BAMPFA/event/331139-film-screening-harakir
 i
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:berkeley-arts
END:VEVENT
