BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Film Screening: The Sword — Berkeley/San Francisco
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-08:00":20261107T183000
DTSTAMP:20261107T130934Z
UID:f382fb2c42000642c469d5471949@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Films\,Berkeley/San Francisco\,United States
DESCRIPTION:An ambitious swordsman looking to bolster his reputation hunts
  for an older master to defeat in a duel. On his quest\, he gets embroiled
  with a young woman chased by bandits (no slouch with a sword herself)\, h
 is childhood sweetheart (unhappily married into wealth)\, and a cursed\, e
 vil sword. Patrick Tam’s iconoclastic convictions are already apparent i
 n this feature debut: “Martial arts films give an impression of being co
 nventional\; I wanted to push the envelope in visual experiment.” The fi
 ght choreography is fluid and fast\, and the film’s expressive use of co
 lor would become one of Tam’s signatures.\nCategory: Films\nOriginal lis
 ting: https://events.berkeley.edu/townsend/event/337295-film-screening-the
 -sword
LOCATION:BAMPFA\, BAMPFA
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://events.berkeley.edu/townsend/event/337295-film-screening-the-s
 word
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:berkeley-arts
END:VEVENT
